more independent variables are used to predict a dependent variable. It helps determine
how several factors simultaneously influence the output.
The mathematical model is expressed as:
Y = b₀ + b₁X₁ + b₂X₂ + ... + bₙXₙ
where Y is the dependent variable, X₁ to Xₙ are the independent variables, and b₀, b₁, ..., bₙ
are regression coefficients.
The algorithm estimates these coefficients using the Least Squares Method, minimizing the
difference between actual and predicted values.
Multiple Linear Regression is widely used when several input variables influence the
outcome. It provides better prediction accuracy than Simple Linear Regression when the
selected features are relevant.
