Algorithm
1. Import the required Python libraries.
2. Load and preprocess the dataset.
3. Separate the feature matrix and class labels.
4. Compute the mean vector for each class.
5. Calculate the within-class scatter matrix.
6. Calculate the between-class scatter matrix.
7. Compute the eigenvalues and eigenvectors.
8. Select the most significant discriminant components.
9. Transform the original dataset into the new feature space.
10. Analyze the transformed data and evaluate classification performance.
Conclusion
In this experiment, Linear Discriminant Analysis was successfully implemented for
dimensionality reduction and classification. The algorithm projected the original dataset
into a lower-dimensional space while maximizing the separation between different classes.
The results demonstrated that LDA is an effective supervised dimensionality reduction
technique that improves classification performance and reduces computational complexity
for machine learning applications.
